  "binding_plan": [
    "Wait for actual original libObj/libgpe loading; resolve real symbols from original handles.",
    "Derive load bias with dladdr/dl_iterate_phdr; discover JUMP_SLOT by exact dynamic symbol. Never subtract A7C2 function offsets or write its GOT offsets.",
    "Initial hooks preserve original call/return, errno, thread ownership and message bytes. They only record first actual UI/GPE events.",
    "After observed initialization, derive each FX3 parameter-block, bitmap handle, allocation bounds and original locks before enabling explicit raster/consumer models.",
    "Use original surface with swap/bitmap/raster/lifetime lease. Atomic private snapshot only after all validations. No ACK before successful retained copy and readback."
  ],
  "public_surface_static_facts": [
    "GRM_screenGetOnBitmap receives output pointer in x0 and stores a raw current bitmap to *x0; it does not AddRef.",
    "GRM_fbrmLockSwap has no input and reaches two original infinite semaphore waits; calling before initialization or on a recursive owning thread can block/assert.",
    "LockSwap implementation uses FX3 framebuffer semaphore objects at +0x88 then +0x78; Unlock reverses. This differs from A7C2 private identity assumptions.",
    "ReadLockBits forwards x1/x2 to bitmap vtable+0x88; this is not sufficient to call arbitrary bitmap classes without checking actual target ABI.",
    "GetSize writes a 64-bit byte length, not framebuffer width/height. Release must not be called on a raw borrowed getter without owning a reference."
  ],
